# wallhack

> **wallhack** (plural **wallhacks**)
>
> *(video games)* A patch enabling a player to cheat by modifying the properties of walls, as by making them transparent or nonsolid.

A Layer 3 tunneling tool built for network pivoting in penetration testing scenarios.

It establishes a full TUN interface on the entry node, routing all traffic transparently — TCP, UDP, ICMP, any protocol — without proxy chains or SOCKS configuration. Tools behave as if they're on the target network.

Built for throughput and operational use. Runs as a single 4 MB binary with no dependencies. REPL and REST API on every entry node for live management.

## Performance and Reliability

Two transports are available: **UDP (QUIC)** and **TCP (WebSocket)**. Both sustain multi-gigabit throughput. WebSocket has lower latency on reliable paths; QUIC holds up better under packet loss with multiple concurrent connections.

{% grid %}
{% card title="UDP (QUIC)" icon="wifi" %}
- **Single stream:** 2.4 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 2.4 Gbps
- **Reverse:** 581 Mbps
- **4 streams @ 2% loss:** 17 Mbps
{% /card %}
{% card title="TCP (WebSocket)" icon="plug" %}
- **Single stream:** 2.4 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 2.5 Gbps
- **Latency:** ~21% lower RTT
- **4 streams @ 2% loss:** 7.7 Mbps
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}

{% callout type="note" %}
Measured with both nodes on the same machine with no real network between them. See [Benchmarks](/benchmarks) for full results including performance on degraded networks.
{% /callout %}

## Management

Every entry node includes a built-in REPL for real-time tunnel management — inspect peers, view active connections, monitor traffic, and adjust routes without restarting. A REST API is also available for programmatic control.

[Management →](/management)

## Binary Size

Distributed as a single static binary with no runtime dependencies. The slim build strips out the REST API and REPL for constrained environments.

| Target | Default | Slim |
|--------|---------|------|
| Linux x64 (glibc) | 6.05 MB | 4.65 MB |
| Linux x64 (musl, static) | 6.01 MB | 4.63 MB |
| Linux arm64 | 5.34 MB | 4.07 MB |

